TwoWheeler TN01A1 -> Rs 30.0
Car TN02B2 -> Rs 90.0
ElectricCar TN03C3 -> Rs 210.0
true
5. Dynamic Method Dispatch Trace
When v.calculateFee(130) is executed:
Declared Reference Type	Actual Object Type	Rate
Vehicle	TwoWheeler	₹10
Vehicle	Car	₹30
Vehicle	ElectricCar	₹30
For 130 minutes, billable hours = 3.
•	TwoWheeler: 3 × 10 = ₹30
•	Car: 3 × 30 = ₹90
•	ElectricCar: (3 × 30) + (10 × 12) = ₹210
The JVM selects the correct overridden ratePerHour() method based on the actual object type.
6. Why Does the Last Line Print true?
The equals() method compares registration numbers.
Both objects have the same registration number TN02B2. Therefore, it returns true.
However, in a real parking system, two different vehicles should not be considered the same vehicle merely because their registration numbers match across different vehicle types. A stricter comparison can also check the vehicle category.
7. Alternative Concept – instanceof vs Dynamic Dispatch
Comparison	Dynamic Dispatch	instanceof and Casting
Method selection	Automatically at runtime	Manually using conditions
Time complexity	O(1)	Up to O(k) checks
Code size	Less code	More if–else conditions
Maintenance	Easy to extend	Difficult when new types are added
Flexibility	High	Lower
